"SHALPAINTS","mcap":691.0,"pdf_link":"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachLive/c33bf3db-acfb-422f-be4e-0b9a0189d650.pdf","ticker":"SHALPAINTS"},{"mcap":null},{"mcap":null},{"mcap":null},{"mcap":null}],"m_and_a":[{"mcap":null},{"company":"Krystal Integrated Services Limited","isin":"INE0QN801017","label":"KRYSTAL","mcap":879.5,"pdf_link":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/KISL123_12082026094503_KISL_Press_release_120826.pdf","ticker":"KRYSTAL"},{"company":"Max Estates Limited","isin":"INE03EI01018","label":"MAXESTATES","mcap":8013.3,"pdf_link":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/MEL_12082026151436_20260812acquisitionofCCDsinMSL.pdf","ticker":"MAXESTATES"},{"company":"Bluspring Enterprises Ltd","isin":"INE0U4101014","label":"BLUSPRING","mcap":1791.2,"pdf_link":"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachLive/ec301715-4320-45bd-9db8-19a62bf7fbf0.pdf","ticker":"BLUSPRING"},{"company":"Shah Alloys Ltd","isin":"INE640C01011","label":"SHAHALLOYS","mcap":159.7,"pdf_link":"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachLive/a874403a-1696-457e-b601-7586567508f0.pdf","ticker":"SHAHALLOYS"},{"mcap":null}],"order_wins":[{"company":"Texmaco Rail & Engineering Ltd","isin":"INE621L01012","label":"TEXRAIL","mcap":4176.5,"pdf_link":"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachLive/7ff51ad5-1cde-4be0-be72-daaee68cc5ca.pdf","ticker":"TEXRAIL"},{"mcap":null},{"company":"Slone Infosystems Limited","isin":"INE0SMA01017","label":"SLONE","mcap":77.8,"pdf_link":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/sloneinfo_12082026154358_Order_Intimation.pdf","ticker":"SLONE"},{"company":"Spice Lounge Food Works Ltd","isin":"","label":"Spice Lounge Food Works Ltd","mcap":1908.0,"pdf_link":"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachLive/f749b46f-5805-497e-a427-f64f70cd931b.pdf","ticker":"SPICELOUNG"},{"mcap":null},{"company":"Viviana Power Tech Limited","isin":"INE0MEG01014","label":"VIVIANA","mcap":698.9,"pdf_link":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/VIVIANA_12082026110832_L1_Intimation.pdf","ticker":"VIVIANA"},{"company":"JSW Infrastructure Ltd","isin":"INE880J01026","label":"JSWINFRA","mcap":76866.8,"pdf_link":"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachLive/dec96194-6129-467b-8324-d6d1a2a6af21.pdf","ticker":"JSWINFRA"},{"mcap":null},{"mcap":null}],"other_notable":[{"mcap":null},{"company":"Switching Technologies Gunther Ltd","isin":"INE311D01017","label":"Switching Technologies Gunther Ltd","mcap":null,"pdf_link":"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachLive/243fdf4d-c41a-4df2-8597-260d07dbc7f4.pdf","ticker":"NAN"},{"mcap":null},{"mcap":null},{"mcap":null}]},"theme_titles":{"business_updates":"Business updates","capex_core":"Capex (core / topline)","distress_risk":"Distress & risk","equity_allotments":"Equity allotments (new)","fund_raises_fresh_equity":"Fund raises (fresh equity)","m_and_a":"M&A / restructuring","order_wins":"Order wins (notable vs mcap)","other_notable":"Other notable"},"themes":{"business_updates":["**Ola Electric** — the Ministry of Heavy Industries revises the **ACC PLI timelines for Ola Cell Technologies**, securing a **five-year window to CY2031 and unlocking up to Rs 7,240 crore of cumulative incentives**, disbursed quarterly _(~39% of mcap)_. The figure is a ceiling contingent on reaching the 20 GWh allocation, not money received.","**Results season, and it is most of the day** — **540 companies filed results, transcripts or presentations**. Per §2 their figures are revenue and profit, not events: **VA Tech Wabag** (Rs 886.8 cr consolidated revenue, PAT Rs 90.1 cr, **order book ~Rs 19,400 cr**), **SEPC** (Rs 282 cr income, a Rs 11 cr net loss) and **Vibhor Steel Tubes** (Rs 293.69 cr).","**Lenskart** — its shareholders' letter reports **same-store sales growth of 18.3%**, self-reported and surfaced by the tier-1 operating gate rather than the RSS subject.","**No commercial terms:** **Thomas Cook (India)** (an India Forex Report launch), **Computer Age Management Services** (an IIT Madras FinTech initiative), **Signet Industries** and **Cineline India** (a three-screen multiplex at Gurugram)."],"capex_core":["**Sambhv Steel Tubes** — receives Environmental Clearance for Unit-3 at Sarora, Raipur, for a **30 MW CAPTIVE power plant at a proposed INR 1,500 million**; **§6 skips captive power** as a cost item rather than core capacity, so it is not a mover.","**Juniper Green Energy** — **commissions an additional 167 MW of wind capacity**, with no project cost stated. **JK Cement** commissions its **J.K. White Nathdwara wall-putty plant**, likewise unvalued.","**Ice Make Refrigeration's Rs 39.00 crore** is an **object of a proposed issue** — *'potential acquisition of new business'* in an EGM corrigendum, alongside Rs 35.28 crore for a JV subscription — not an announced transaction.","**No material rupee commitment stated:** **Multi Commodity Exchange** (a proposed mineral spot exchange), **Mukta Arts**, **Tinna Rubber** (a Saudi wholly-owned subsidiary), **Natural Capsules**, **Prostarm** (an MoA alteration) and **Kay Power and Paper**."],"distress_risk":["**Elpro International** — files the **Post Offer Public Announcement declaring its voluntary BSE delisting offer successful**, by acquirers I G E (India) and Zenox Technology Services with Surbhit and Yamini Dabriwala as persons acting in concert.","**Nova Iron & Steel** — the **Section 7 IBC application filed against the company was dismissed**, the one clearly favourable insolvency outcome on the tape. **HCL Infosystems** reports a **favourable CESTAT Allahabad order**.","**Associated Alcohols & Breweries** — the **Madhya Pradesh High Court stays an FSSAI order**; **Matrimony.com** reports a Madras High Court order in a trademark suit brought by Free Elective Network; **neither quantifies the impact**.","**Show-cause notices and CoC business, none quantified:** **Ucal** (GST audit), **ZF Commercial Vehicle Control Systems**, **SKIL Infrastructure** (ninth CoC meeting), **Reliance Communications** (CoC on 13-Aug), **McNally Bharat**, **Unitech International** and **Birla Corporation**."],"equity_allotments":["**UVS Hospitality and Services** — allots **23,87,257 equity shares at Rs 100, Rs 23.87 crore, for consideration other than cash**, completing the **share-swap acquisition of 34.76% of Calcio Restaurants**, plus 2,16,000 cash shares and 4,45,000 warrants.","**Pune E-Stock Broking** — converts **7,61,000 warrants into equity, Rs 9.76 crore** _(~2.4% of mcap)_. **Fischer Medical Ventures** (Rs 11.64 cr) and **Rekvina Laboratories** (Rs 4.63 cr) filed conversions and a preferential allotment on the same day.","**Audroc** — allots **3,75,00,000 fully convertible equity warrants to a single allottee**, with **no rupee value in the intimation**, so nothing is published. **Ajooni Biotech's** 90,00,000-security allotment is held out on a content mismatch."],"fund_raises_fresh_equity":["**Shalimar Paints** — alongside the swap above, the same board approved **Rs 105.86 crore of preferential equity for cash at Rs 85 to non-promoter allottees** and **a QIP of up to Rs 1,000 crore**, both subject to shareholders.","**Prostarm Info Systems** — **29,43,717 fully convertible warrants at Rs 147, Rs 43.27 crore**, to non-promoter investors on a preferential basis _(~5.0% of mcap; new warrants, §4)_.","**A raise WITHDRAWN, which is the opposite of one.** **SBC Exports' board approved the withdrawal and cancellation of its proposed preferential issue of equity shares**, yet the row reached the store as a **Rs 99.06 crore `fund_raise`** _(the Garnet family, 11-Aug)_.","**Brookfield India Real Estate Trust's Rs 1,700 crore** is a **REIT** disclosure — trust capital recycling, demoted under §3 — as are **Embassy Office Parks REIT's Rs 400 crore**, **Maple Infrastructure Trust**, **Cube Highways Trust** and **Interise Trust**.","**Earlier stages, no size stated:** **Texmo Pipes** (Rs 6.98 cr preferential), **Chemiesynth (Vapi)**, **Finkurve Financial**, **63 Moons** (a raise at subsidiary Ticker Limited), **GMR Airports** and **Magellanic Cloud** (an amendment to its issue objects)."],"m_and_a":["**UltraTech Cement / Waaree Energies — one deal, filed from both sides.** UltraTech subscribes **26% of Solaris Horizon Energy, a Waaree wholly-owned subsidiary, for Rs 27,75,50,000 in cash** alongside an Energy Supply Agreement, closing within 180 days _(0.01% of UltraTech's mcap)_.","**Krystal Integrated Services** — acquires **100% of Citelum India from the EDF Group** to hold it as a wholly-owned subsidiary in city and street lighting; **the release states no consideration**, so no rupee figure is published here.","**Max Estates** — subsidiary **Max Square allotted 8,75,09,608 shares on conversion of Series A and B CCDs** held by Max Estates and New York Life; **Max Estates' stake stays at ~51% with no change in control**, so the Rs 1,104.82 cr recall figure is not a consideration.","**Bluspring Enterprises** — amalgamates **Bluspring New Horizon One into STEAG Energy Services (India)**, both wholly-owned; the **Rs 537.70 crore is the transferee's FY26 turnover**, not a price, and the transaction is exempt as an intra-group deal.","**Shah Alloys** — a **strategic review and proposed restructuring or monetisation of the Santej steel plant**, whose operations the board resolved to close in July 2025 as the machinery had aged and the technology become obsolete; **no value stated**.","**No consideration or swap ratio stated:** **Coal India** (a non-binding MoU with ArcelorMittal Nippon Steel India), **SecMark Consultancy** (amalgamating Codifi Finserv), **Dixon Technologies**, **Raymond Realty**, **Lenskart**, **N2N Technologies**, **Race Eco Chain** and **Mallcom (India)**."],"order_wins":["**Texmaco Rail & Engineering** — a **Rs 77.76 crore purchase order from IVC Logistics** for three rakes of ACT1 wagons, each with one BVCM wagon _(~1.8% of mcap, the narrowest §5 pass on the tape)_.","**B.R. Goyal Infrastructure** — separately from its warrant allotment above, an **NHAI work order at Rs 39,00,22,575** for engagement as **user-fee agency at the Husnapur toll plaza, Maharashtra**, won by e-tender _(~8.6% of mcap)_.","**Slone Infosystems** — **Rs 10.07 crore including GST** for **500 i5 laptops (Rs 1.02 cr) and 5,000 i3 desktops (Rs 8.41 cr)** with three months' extended warranty, to be executed within 30 days _(~13.2% of mcap)_.","**Spice Lounge Food Works** — a live-events contract from **Xora World** with an aggregate value **in excess of Rs 21 crore** over four months, which its release also frames as anticipated revenue potential _(~1.2% of mcap)_.","**Diamond Power Infrastructure** — a **Rs 61.04 crore Letter of Intent from Purvanchal Vidyut Vitran Nigam** for 33 kV HT XLPE cable, which at **0.32% of a Rs 19,076 cr market cap fails §5** and is not surfaced as a mover.","**Viviana Power Tech** — **L1 bid confirmation, not an award**, at **Rs 113 crore inclusive of taxes** for MVCC overhead conversion and underground networking for MGVCL _(demoted per the GPT Infraprojects ruling of 06-Aug)_.","**JSW Infrastructure** — signs the **concession agreement with Syama Prasad Mookerjee Port Authority, Kolkata** for the outer container terminal and berths 1-5 at Netaji Subhash Dock, following its 09-Jun LoA; **no project cost is stated**.","**Already published — SEPC.** Its results release restates the **4.2 MTPA SAIL-IISCO Burnpur pellet-plant package at Rs 952.19 crore**, published on **05-Aug at Rs 854.57 crore net of input tax credit**; the release does not reconcile the two bases.","**No value stated, so not surfaced (§3):** **Mayasheel Ventures**, **Ahasolar Technologies**, **Dhanashree Electronics** and **AVG Logistics**."],"other_notable":["**Ambalal Sarabhai Enterprises — the store's Rs 81.99 crore 'JV' is Rs 81.99 LAKH**, the one-time **New Labour Codes provision** booked as an exceptional item in its results; the row carried it as a jv_agreement at 23.29% of market cap.","**Switching Technologies Gunther** — a **Rs 50 crore buyback figure at 181.8% of a Rs 27.50 crore market cap** sits on a row the store itself flags as a content mismatch; **the cached filing does not support it**, so no figure is published.","**Credit-rating actions are theme-only and never movers (§3), and these are facility sizes rather than events:** **Vikram Solar Rs 4,000 crore**, **Huhtamaki India Rs 200 crore** and **Jay Ushin Rs 63.49 crore**. None states a notch change in the intimation.","**Splits are never movers (§6):** **Bansal Wire Industries** alters its capital clause for a sub-division and **TD Power Systems** fixes the record date for its stock split. **Paisalo Digital** held an FCCB committee meeting.","**Shareholding and SAST disclosures (names only, §1):** 28 rows, including Vedanta, Mahindra & Mahindra, Emami, Inox Wind and Star Health. The detail is deliberately not carried."]},"unlocks":[{"company":"Hindustan Foods Limited","date":"2026-08-12","days":0,"detail":"Scheme of amalgamation listed · allotted 21-05-2026","instrument_id":"13039","mcap":7685.7,"pct":28.72,"pct_of":"equity","shares":48139085,"src":"BSE+NSE","symbol":"HNDFDS","type":"AMALGAMATION","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/downloads/UploadDocs/Notices/20260811-23/20260811-23.pdf"},{"company":"Citizen Solar Limited","date":"2026-08-12","days":0,"detail":"Scheme of amalgamation listed · allotted 03-04-2026","instrument_id":"14314","mcap":330.9,"pct":61.57,"pct_of":"equity","shares":8646000,"src":"BSE","symbol":"CITIZEN","type":"AMALGAMATION","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/downloads/UploadDocs/Notices/20260811-24/20260811-24.pdf"},{"company":"LLOYDS ENGINEERING WORKS LIMITED","date":"2026-08-12","days":0,"detail":"Conversion listed","instrument_id":"10843","mcap":13570.4,"pct":null,"pct_of":"equity","shares":14714074,"src":"BSE+NSE","symbol":"LLOYDSENGG","type":"CONVERSION","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/downloads/UploadDocs/Notices/20260811-28/20260811-28.pdf"},{"comp